-- title:
--   Strong approximation at v from connectedness of the class-set graph
-- statement:
--   Fix $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ and let $R$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of the quaternion algebra $\mathbb{H}=\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ which is an order, i.e. contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, spans $\mathbb{H}$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ and is finitely generated. Let $r$ be a prime, $v$ a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ containing $r$, and let $n$ be a unit of $\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q},f}$ lying in `primeHeckeSet R r`: both $n$ and $r\cdot n^{-1}$ lie in the finite adelic box of $R$ (the additive group generated by the $z\otimes\alpha$ with $z\in R$ and $\alpha$ integral at every place), while $n^{-1}$ and $r^{-1}\cdot n$ do not. Assume the connectedness hypothesis: every subset $P$ of the double coset space $\mathbb{H}^{\times}\backslash(\mathbb{H}\otimes\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q},f})^{\times}/\mathrm{Stab}(R)$, where $\mathrm{Stab}(R)$ is the group of adelic units preserving the box of $R$, such that for every class $e$ modulo $\mathrm{Stab}(R\cap nRn^{-1})$ the class of a representative $e$ lies in $P$ if and only if the class of that representative times $n$ lies in $P$, is either empty or everything. Then every unit $x$ of $\mathbb{H}\otimes\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q},f}$ factors as $x=\gamma\, g\, u$ with $\gamma\in\mathbb{H}^{\times}$ embedded diagonally, $u\in\mathrm{Stab}(R)$, and $g$ having component $1$ in $\mathbb{H}\otimes\mathbb{Q}_{w}$ at every place $w\neq v$.
--
--   This is the strong approximation statement $\widehat{\mathbb{H}}^{\times}=\mathbb{H}^{\times}\cdot\mathbb{H}_{v}^{\times}\cdot\widehat{R}^{\times}$, derived here from connectedness of the graph on the class set of $R$ whose edges are indexed by the class set of $R\cap nRn^{-1}$ with the two degeneracy maps (the Brandt, or Hecke, graph at $r$). It is used in the Eichler-order case, in [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsEichlerOrder.exists_eq_finiteIdeleDiagonal_mul_mul_of_squarefree_of_not_dvd`](thm.html#QuaternionAlgebra.IsEichlerOrder.exists_eq_finiteIdeleDiagonal_mul_mul_of_squarefree_of_not_dvd), where the hypotheses on the level and the ramification prime are available.
-- source:
